Third-party data
----------------
The test fixtures (tests/fixtures) include data from outside sources, kept so the tests run offline:
- tests/fixtures/recorded-seeds.json: advisory records from the GitHub Advisory Database
  (https://github.com/github/advisory-database), licensed CC-BY-4.0, as served by OSV.dev. One of them, the
  PyJWT advisory GHSA-ffqj-6fqr-9h24, quotes an example EC private key in its text: it is the advisory's own
  example, not a secret of this project (.gitleaksignore records it).
- tests/fixtures/real/: output of Trivy (https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy) and Grype
  (https://github.com/anchore/grype) for public images, which repeats advisory text from the US National
  Vulnerability Database (public domain), the GitHub Advisory Database (CC-BY-4.0), Red Hat security data
  (CC-BY-4.0), and the Debian and Ubuntu security trackers.
src/oss_intake/cvss.py follows the CVSS v3.1 specification by FIRST (https://www.first.org/cvss/), including its
Appendix A rounding function. CVSS is a trademark of FIRST.
Data fetched at run time is listed, with its terms, in docs/guide.md ("Data sources and their terms").
